{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1021589-characters-with-multiple-orders","id":1021589,"title":"Characters with multiple Orders","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-24T09:14:37-08:00","id":1021589,"title":"Characters with multiple Orders","content":"In order to appease my taste for hybrid and generalist characters, let's discuss the characters that belong in multiple Orders, by developing Order Status in more than one Order. It is assumed that by expending the experience to buy such Merits, they have effectively dealt with the social drawbacks of their divided loyalties as it concerns making the character viable and manageable (it is of course OK and part of the purpose of the exercise if they become a recurrent plot hook), at least until they go and teach trade secrets to non-members.<br /> <br /> Which Order combinations would you deem especially cool, useful, and thematically feasible ? As for myself, I find the 'Indiana Jones' combo of Arrow and Mysterium especially cool and thematically quite compatible, and the mix of Adamant Hand and Egregore rather useful. From a thematic PoV, I find the combination of either with Silver Ladder just as interesting, although Lex Magica is much less useful. From a strict optimization viewpoint, a forbidden fruit is to combine any of Arrow, Mysterium, or Silver Ladder with a Seer Prelacy (especially the Crowns of Doctrine, Fury, or Obligation), but such a character would of course be unfeasible, short of playing a mole or defector (e.g. an interesting idea might be a Seer defector to the Diamond that is tormented by her old Exarch master due to her Prelacy bonds).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 12-24-2016, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T10:10:47-08:00","id":1021604,"title":"","content":"You don't need to be in an Order to have Order Status since it can also function as having standing in or respect from an Order. For instance, with an Adamantine Arrow that's well known for his service to the Silver Ladder run Consilium it wouldn't be too surprising to find out that they taught him the Lex Magica Merit. So whatever on that front.<br /> <br /> The whole point of doing something like this, other than the mechanical benefits, is the social drawbacks of divided loyalties. If you want to just ignore that part then you're ignoring at least part of your actual story building potential for a gimmick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 12-24-2016, 01:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T10:17:01-08:00","id":1021606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1021589-characters-with-multiple-orders?p=1021604#post1021604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't need to be in an Order to have Order Status since it can also function as having standing in or respect from an Order. For instance, with an Adamantine Arrow that's well known for his service to the Silver Ladder run Consilium it wouldn't be too surprising to find out that they taught him the Lex Magica Merit. So whatever on that front.<br /> <br /> The whole point of doing something like this, other than the mechanical benefits, is the social drawbacks of divided loyalties. If you want to just ignore that part then you're ignoring at least part of your actual story building potential for a gimmick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I mis-explained myself. I do not mean to rule out the social effects of divided loyalties as a recurrent/occasional plot hook. This is indeed part of the point of the exercise, I meant to say it is assumed they do not get so severe as to make the character unviable and unmanageable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 12-24-2016, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T10:27:03-08:00","id":1021613,"title":"","content":"I play a libertine who left the Guardians on good terms (and having passed his veils), retaining a dot of Guardian status. My game doesn't let me keep Guardian merits (and I probably wouldn't anyway), but his mystery cult is still connected with the Labyrinth.<br /> <br /> I find it a fun combination. He still believes a lot of Guardian orthodoxy (especially re paradox) and it helps that the local caucus is fairly sympathetic to Sleepers. Mostly it provides complications and access to tip-offs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T11:47:10-08:00","id":1021630,"title":"","content":"It would be interesting to play a deep-cover Guardian with a Masque that's a member of a different Order, taking their Status and Order Merit with Masque 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T14:49:17-08:00","id":1021709,"title":"","content":"I imagine there's a decent amount of bleedover between the Guardians and the Arrow in terms of membership, as both are focused on the immediate physical threats that threaten sleepers and their consilias. When some idiot summons an Abyssal horror downtown, both of them likely work together to kill/bind/banish the damn thing and contain the collateral damage that results, resulting in a lot of camaraderie and owed favors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T00:01:42-08:00","id":1021871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1021589-characters-with-multiple-orders?p=1021613#post1021613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I play a libertine who left the Guardians on good terms (and having passed his veils), retaining a dot of Guardian status. My game doesn't let me keep Guardian merits (and I probably wouldn't anyway), but his mystery cult is still connected with the Labyrinth.<br /> <br /> I find it a fun combination. He still believes a lot of Guardian orthodoxy (especially re paradox) and it helps that the local caucus is fairly sympathetic to Sleepers. Mostly it provides complications and access to tip-offs.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you paid Xp for Guardian Merits, learned them in good standing, and left on good terms, I see no good reason why you shouldn't keep them. Sanctity of Merits and this is part of the purpose of the exercise, and it is not like the character can un-learn techniques.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 12-25-2016, 04:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T15:02:52-08:00","id":1022100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1021589-characters-with-multiple-orders?p=1021871#post1021871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you paid Xp for Guardian Merits, learned them in good standing, and left on good terms, I see no good reason why you shouldn't keep them. Sanctity of Merits and this is part of the purpose of the exercise, and it is not like the character can un-learn techniques.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if you didn't leave on good terms, well... that's what Mind magic is for. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":